+## 1. Regex and recursive readonly trees now compose on the scratch merge
+
+The proving program `gaps/1_regex_and_value_tree.ts` prints `Parsed` and `Ok`
+on Node, native and the JavaScript backend. The compiler proof on
+`codex/regex-cycle-proof` recognizes supported regex IR operations without
+weakening cycle-capable user slots, and evaluates their operands for effects.
+The complete `compose_main.ts` is held natively against Go on all 24,076
+CSS/SCSS inputs, with sanitizers and the leak check. No tree child field became
+Weak. The gap test now checks backend and memory agreement rather than a refusal.
+
+Current main lacks this branch's native regex lowering and emission. The scratch
+merge also adapts the older regex shape initializers to main's shape layout.
+These are integration dependencies, not remaining cycle-proof gaps. Evidence and
+the integration patch are in `docs/regex-cycle-proof.md` on the proof branch.
 
